## Work-only Pi Skills

Private work skills must stay out of this public chezmoi repository. Create or update them in `~/code/work-scripts/pi-skills/<skill-name>/`, commit and push the private repository, then reconcile packaged skills with:

```bash
chezmoi apply --source-path "$HOME/.local/share/chezmoi/.chezmoiscripts/run_after_11-update-work-scripts.sh.tmpl"
```

Do not add public per-skill `symlink_*` entries for private skills. The packaged reconciler owns links via `${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/chezmoi/work-pi-skills.manifest` and preserves unrelated/personal skills.

## Work Commit Messages

- Format: `<ticket>: <single line description>`, e.g. `BLOB-1234: add retry to chunk upload`.
- One line only: no body, no bullet lists, no semicolons or other multi-clause chaining. Keep the description short, lowercase and imperative, with no full stop.
- Take the ticket key from the branch name, bookmark, or user; ask if unknown.
- Before writing any work commit message, PR title or description, review reply or code comment, read `~/.pi/agent/skills/adam-writing-style/SKILL.md` and follow it. Delegated agents that write such text must do the same.
